cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use Primus Decision 0.1 in your work, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "Primus Decision 0.1 (Research Alpha): an open 3.7M-parameter non-transformer model for typed probabilistic decisions"
version: "0.1"
date-released: "2026-09-23"
license: Apache-2.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/pally-sai-tilak/primus-decision"
authors:
  - family-names: "Pally"
    given-names: "Sai Tilak"
    affiliation: "AAME"
  - name: "AAME"
keywords:
  - typed decisions
  - probabilistic decisions
  - calibration
  - state-space model
  - GRU
  - CPU inference
abstract: >-
  Primus Decision 0.1 answers typed questions about a JSON state with probability distributions: whether a statement
  is true, which of the offered options applies, which level on an ordinal scale. It is an ensemble of a diagonal
  state-space (S4D) encoder and a bidirectional GRU with LSA case features, 3,715,074 neural parameters in total, run
  on a CPU. On the official test split of LocalLLaMA/typed-decisions it reached accuracy 0.751, Brier 0.059 and ECE
  0.127 in one sealed run after freezing; the Laya reference reaches accuracy 0.766 under the same protocol.
